Use MIT-SHM 1.2 (fd passing) with POSIX shm instead of SysV shm.

xcb owns the fd passed to xcb_shm_attach_fd() and closes it after
sending it, so it must not be closed again later.  The mapping comes
from mmap(2), so release it with munmap(2) rather than shmdt(2).
Only use SHM if the server supports MIT-SHM 1.2 and the connection
is a unix domain socket.

